(Title) Tj
T*
(Nationwide telemetry-based cardiac arrhythmia screening in older adults: findings from a) Tj
T*
(large pragmatic trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Systematic identification of previously undiscovered atrial fibrillation in) Tj
T*
(at-risk populations remains challenging despite its implications for stroke prevention.) Tj
T*
(Methods: We enrolled 50,549 adults aged 65 and older with at least one clinical marker for) Tj
T*
(thromboembolism risk through a fully automated digital platform. Participants were) Tj
T*
(randomly assigned to receive remote ECG telemetry surveillance or standard clinical care.) Tj
T*
(The telemetry group underwent 7 days of continuous electrocardiographic monitoring using a) Tj
T*
(wearable patch system mailed directly to their homes. Results: Among participants) Tj
T*
(allocated to telemetry, 1.9% were found to have previously unidentified atrial) Tj
T*
(fibrillation. Of these newly detected cases, approximately 96% of patients initiated) Tj
T*
(appropriate anticoagulation management following recommendations to their primary care) Tj
T*
(providers. No serious adverse events related to the screening process were reported.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Large-scale, remotely administered ECG screening is operationally feasible and) Tj
T*
(identifies clinically relevant arrhythmia in a significant proportion of older individuals) Tj
T*
(at baseline thrombotic risk, with high uptake of guideline-directed medical therapy.) Tj
